https://www.morfrac.com/blog/custom-6/40000-times-its-weight-15,https://www.morfrac.com/blog/custom-6/40000-times-its-weight-15,200,0.48,,MORFRAC | Custom. Blocks,24,"Discover Custom Titanium morfblock. MORFRAC's ultra-light yet powerful morfblock. inspired by the diabolical ironclad beetle. Withstand up to 40,000 times its weight in SWL, blending strength and compact design for unmatched durability.",236,https://www.morfrac.com/blog/custom-6/40000-times-its-weight-15,,True,technical_blog,medium,high,medium,low,2,"40,000 times its weight",9,776,"Skip to Content Follow us Click here to setup your social networks 0 My Cart 0 Wishlist Sign in HOME MORFRAC PRODUCTS powerfurl. morfblock. padeye. morfwing. morfring. dogbone. Ti-shackle. custom. SOLUTIONS SHOP STORIES PARTNERS CONTACT Shop Now! 0 0 HOME MORFRAC PRODUCTS powerfurl. morfblock. padeye. morfwing. morfring. dogbone. Ti-shackle. custom. SOLUTIONS SHOP STORIES PARTNERS CONTACT Follow us Click here to setup your social networks Sign in Shop Now! 40,000 times its weight morfblock.[beetle] 31 January 2024 by MORFRAC SYSTEMS S.L., Raffaele De Rose In the world of the truly extraordinary, there's an unassuming powerhouse: the diabolical ironclad beetle . This pint-sized super-beetle is about as tough as nature gets, capable of withstanding an astonishing 40,000 times its body weight . To put that into perspective, imagine a beetle in a tiny weightlifting suit, hefting around a tank. While the US Air Force studies its indestructibility for insights into tougher armor, at MORFRAC we’ve taken a page from the beetle’s playbook in our morfblock. - engineered to perform under Herculean stress, just like our durable little friend. Now, let's backtrack to a couple of months ago, when we were approached with a request so bold it almost rivaled the beetle’s feat. The client asked for something insanely powerful but whisper-light , possibly blue and, for an added twist, it had to be compact . Our challenge was clear: build something tiny that could still handle tens of thousands of times its own weight. And that’s when our own “ironclad beetle” moment happened. We engineered this 2t SWL morfblock.[custom] MB Custom to handle insane WL – 40,000 times its own weight, to be exact – in a package that’s only 50g!!! We applied engineering wizardry with a hearty dose of “what if?"". The result? a block that defies expectations on every level, proving that sometimes, just like in nature, great strength really does come in small packages. So the next time you see a beetle ambling by, give it a little nod of respect. That little guy may just be carrying the blueprint for some of the toughest, lightest hardware we’ll ever build. in CUSTOM # morfblock. Labels morfblock. Archive All dates January
