nvented. mreel. is a compact, smart, and ultralight reeler system designed to streamline deck organisation and reduce risk during manoeuvres. Engineered for seamless integration into any sailing setup, its sleek design, non-corrosive materials, and intuitive self-assembly make it an essential addition to modern sailing hardware. Whether you're managing halyard tails, control lines, or spare rope ends, mreel. delivers a clean and tidy solution in seconds. The system features a pump-action ratchet or automatic operation for fast retrieval and spooling, so your cockpit stays safe and clutter-free, even under pressure. Made using precision 3D printing and high-end composites, mreel. is lightweight yet durable, easy to install with common adhesives, and requires no structural modifications. Its modular range covers boats from under 35’ to over 65’, with shared spare parts and upgrade options for maximum versatility. This isn’t just a rope reeler. It’s a practical innovation that transforms the way you sail. mreel.[one] mreel.[two] mreel.[three] mreel.[four] Boat LOA Sub 35’ 35–50’ 50–65’ 65’+ Max Line Length* 24 m 34 m 36 m 42 m Max Line Ø* 7–8 mm 8 mm 9 mm 12 mm Auto Option Yes Yes Yes No Weight 690 g 730 g 770 g 1175 g Dimensions 195 × 246 × 226 mm 210 × 300 × 290 mm 210 × 321 × 300 mm 257 × 382 × 360 mm *Max values using Marlow rope. Installation Guide Your Dynamic Snippet will be displayed here...
